      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-8083",
        "knowledge_point_id": "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f",
        "knowledge_point": "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/83c490278bec718da1338f8926e9d67d2f72909487b9a85bbd386cbf72def2bb.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places.",
        "worked_solution": "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-4+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})| \\\\  & ≈2.897.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\theta =2.897$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
