    {
      "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375",
      "id": "q-147561",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": null,
      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-147561",
        "knowledge_point_id": "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747",
        "knowledge_point": "Determining the Image of an Object Formed by a Singular Transformation",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/d88ae8667df81624f0a28295c980f846ae88e9b4766fe0d0f692dd75509a56e9.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 20 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,4)$, $(5,20)$, and  $(2,8).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/94247512fd446447144d808c76d00bc9c0d50d4175697597360117eca00b3cf1.png)",
