        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose",
        "problem": "Which of the following gives the area bounded by the graph of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}?$",
        "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
