      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-67493",
        "knowledge_point_id": "43dcbb7e-ba21-506f-a706-bfb28371e0a9",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the First Term Smaller Than a Given Value",
        "problem": "What is the first term that is less than $0.000\\,6$ in the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n64,\\,32,\\,16,\\,8,\\,…\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=64$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{32}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $n$th term of the sequence can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={2}^{6}\\cdot {2}^{1-n} \\\\  & ={2}^{7-n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want the $n$th term to be less than $0.000\\,6.$\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & <0.000\\,6 \\\\ {2}^{7-n} & <0.000\\,6 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡{(2)}^{7-n} & <\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6) \\\\ (7-n)\\operatorname{log}⁡(2) & <\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6) \\\\ 7-n & <\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)} \\\\ -n & <\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}-7 \\\\ n & >7-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEstimating the right-hand side using a calculator, we get:\n\n$$\n7-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,6)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}≈17.703\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $18$th term is the first term of the sequence that is less than $0.000\\,6.$",
