        "problem": "What is the first term that is less than $0.000\\,08$ in the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n256,\\,64,\\,16,\\,4,\\,…\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=256$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{64}{256}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $n$th term of the sequence can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =256\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={4}^{4}\\cdot {4}^{1-n} \\\\  & ={4}^{5-n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want the $n$th term to be less than $0.000\\,08.$\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & <0.000\\,08 \\\\ {4}^{5-n} & <0.000\\,08 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡({4}^{5-n}) & <\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,08) \\\\ (5-n)\\operatorname{log}⁡(4) & <\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,08) \\\\ 5-n & <\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,08)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)} \\\\ -n & <\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,08)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)}-5 \\\\ n & >5-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,08)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEstimating the right-hand side using a calculator, we get:\n\n$$\n5-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.000\\,08)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)}≈11.805\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $12$th term is the first term of the sequence that is less than $0.000\\,08.$",
